# 1. Different types of tesla cars

### Delivery Trends of Affordable vs Luxury Tesla Models in the Global Market (2019-2024)

```{r, message=FALSE, warning=FALSE, results='hide'}

# Check column names
#colnames(tesla)

# Fix column name spaces
colnames(tesla) <- trimws(colnames(tesla))

# Convert Year to integer (to prevent filtering errors)
tesla$year <- as.integer(trimws(tesla$year))

# Data cleaning
tesla_clean <- tesla %>%
  filter(!is.na(year), year >= 2019 & year <= 2024) %>%
  select(year, model, units.delivered) %>%
  mutate(Category = case_when(
    model %in% c("Model 3", "Model Y") ~ "Affordable",
    model %in% c("Model X", "Model S", "Cybertruck") ~ "Luxury",
    TRUE ~ "Other"
  )) %>%
  filter(Category != "Other")

# Summary
delivery_summary <- tesla_clean %>%
  group_by(year, Category) %>%
  summarise(Total_Deliveries = sum(units.delivered, na.rm = TRUE)) %>%
  ungroup()

# Plot
ggplot(delivery_summary, aes(x = factor(year), y = Total_Deliveries, fill = Category)) +
  geom_col(position = "dodge") +
  geom_text(
    aes(label = scales::comma(Total_Deliveries)),
    position = position_dodge(width = 0.9),
    vjust = -0.3,
    size = 3.5
  ) +
  scale_fill_manual(values = c("#1f77b4", "#ff7f0e")) +
  labs(
    title = "Tesla Deliveries Comparison: Affordable vs Luxury Models (2019–2024)",
    subtitle = "Affordable: Model 3 & Model Y | Luxury: Model X, Model S, Cybertruck",
    x = "Year",
    y = "Total Deliveries (Units)",
    fill = "Vehicle Category"
  ) +
  theme_minimal(base_size = 14) +
  theme(
    plot.title = element_text(face = "bold"),
    legend.position = "top"
  )
delivery_summary
```

#### **Insights:** From the chart, we can observe that affordable car deliveries decreased steadily until 2022 and then increasing steadily agian from 157, 375 units to 218, 813 units in 2024. Meanwhile, luxury cars experienced strong growth until 2022, reaching a peak of 327,073 units, then declined from 2022 to 2023 before recovering to 326,359 units in 2024.

#### **Recommendations:** Based on the bar chart analysis, we recommend that Tesla continue investing in affordable vehicle segments while not neglecting the budget EV market. Additionally, the company should focus on analyzing different luxury models to identify which ones boost deliveries and which ones hinder growth.

